# ...but the synthetic sample set is meant to be here
!1. Local CSV/sample-data/*.csv
!1. Local CSV/sample-data/cowork-tasks/*.csv
# App Edition: its source folder and its bundled synthetic sample
!app/src/data/
!app/public/sample/*.csv
# Fabric App: its rayfin/data folder is source code (table schemas), not an export
!fabric-app/rayfin/data/

# OS / editor
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
desktop.ini
.vscode/
.idea/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# Fabric notebook checkpoints
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# PBIP working projects. The deliverables are the .pbit files, not the projects.
# A project keeps parameter VALUES on disk, so committing one publishes whatever
# tenant identifiers or local paths were last used. A .pbit does not - template
# export strips every parameter value. Two projects reached a commit this way.
*.pbip
*.Report/
*.SemanticModel/
.pbi-work/
